---@class gcp.iamcredentials_v1.GenerateIdTokenResponse
---@field token? string The OpenId Connect ID token. The token is a JSON Web Token (JWT) that contains a payload with claims. See the [JSON Web Token spec](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7519) for more information. Here is an example of a decoded JWT payload: ``` { "iss": "https://accounts.google.com", "iat": 1496953245, "exp": 1496953245, "aud": "https://www.example.com", "sub": "107517467455664443765", "azp": "107517467455664443765", "email": "my-iam-account@my-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com", "email_verified": true, "google": { "organization_number": 123456 } } ```

